#: ../../flying.rst:2
msgid "Flying Tips"
msgstr "ఎగిరే చిట్కాలు"

#: ../../flying.rst:5
msgid "Data collection effort, full 3D"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:7
msgid ""
"For best in class results with full 3D reconstruction, we recommend the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:9
#, python-format
msgid "60% overlap nadir flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:10
#, python-format
msgid "70-80% overlap 45-degree gimbal angle cross-grid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:12
msgid ""
"The 45-degree cross-grid flight provides the basis for a fully tied together "
"model, while the nadir flights provide the necessary texture for orthophoto "
"texturing. The lower overlap  meets the minimum requirement for orthophoto "
"products as facilitated by feature matching from the much higher overlap "
"cross-grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:15
msgid "Data collection effort, 2D and 2.5D products"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:17
msgid ""
"For best in class results 2D and 2.5D products, we recommend the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:19
#, python-format
msgid "70-80% overlap slightly off-nadir (5-10 degree off nadir)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:21
#, python-format
msgid ""
"For more complex buildings and vegetation, aim for closer to 80-83% overlap. "
"If buildings, vegetation, and terrain changes are not complex, it's quite "
"feasible to use closer to 70% overlap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:23
msgid ""
"(credit: derived from ongoing conversations with Ivan Gayton, Humanitarian "
"OpenStreetMap Team)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:26
msgid "Other resources on flying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../flying.rst:28
msgid ""
"The `Humanitarian OpenStreetMap team <https://www.hotosm.org/>`_ has "
"guidelines on `flying for UAV mapping <https://uav-"
"guidelines.openaerialmap.org/>`_:"
msgstr ""
"`హ్యూమానిటేరియన్ ఓపెన్‌స్ట్రీట్ మ్యాప్ బృందం <https://www.hotosm.org/>`_ UAV మ్యాపింగ్ కోసం "
"ఎగురుతున్నందుకు మార్గదర్శకాలను కలిగి ఉంది <https://uav-guidelines.openaerialmap.org/"
">`_:"

#: ../../flying.rst:30
msgid ""
"`Choosing the right UAV <https://uav-guidelines.openaerialmap.org/pages/05-"
"choosing-the-right-uav/>`_"
msgstr ""
"`సరైన UAV ని ఎంచుకోవడం <https://uav-guidelines.openaerialmap.org/pages/05-"
"choosing-the-right-uav/>`_"

#: ../../flying.rst:32
msgid ""
"`Choosing the right sensor <https://uav-guidelines.openaerialmap.org/pages/"
"06-choosing-the-sensor/>`_"
msgstr ""
"`సరైన సెన్సార్‌ను ఎంచుకోవడం <https://uav-guidelines.openaerialmap.org/pages/06-"
"choosing-the-sensor/>`_"

#: ../../flying.rst:34
msgid ""
"`Mission preparation <https://uav-guidelines.openaerialmap.org/pages/07-"
"preparing-for-the-uav-mission/>`_"
msgstr ""
"`మిషన్ తయారీ <https://uav-guidelines.openaerialmap.org/pages/07-preparing-for-"
"the-uav-mission/>` _"

#: ../../flying.rst:36
msgid ""
"The guidelines are intended for drone mapping projects on islands, but have "
"general use for all drone mappers."
msgstr ""
"మార్గదర్శకాలు ద్వీపాలలో డ్రోన్ మ్యాపింగ్ ప్రాజెక్టుల కోసం ఉద్దేశించబడ్డాయి, కానీ అన్ని డ్రోన్ మ్యాపర్‌లకు సాధారణ "
"ఉపయోగం ఉంది."

#: ../../flying.rst:38
msgid ""
"See also DroneDeploy's guide on `Making Successful Maps <https://"
"support.dronedeploy.com/docs/making-successful-maps>`_, which provides great "
"tips on mission planning."
msgstr ""
"మిషన్ ప్లానింగ్‌పై గొప్ప చిట్కాలను అందించే `విజయవంతమైన మ్యాప్‌లను రూపొందించడం <https://"
"support.dronedeploy.com/docs/making-successful-maps>` _ పై డ్రోన్‌డెప్లోయ్ గైడ్ కూడా "
"చూడండి."

